  Inductor/Triton (BSD-3-Clause / MIT) so that their outputs are bit-identical; they are independent TileLang
  implementations, and those projects are credited here for the formats and algorithms they define.
- nvidia-sm120/tilelang_contrib/third_party/tilelang/ holds two unmodified TileLang files
  (examples/gemm_sm120/sm120_nvfp4_blockscaled_gemm.py, maint/gemm/gemm_sm120/tilelang_nvfp4_quantizer.py) under
  TileLang's MIT License, Copyright (c) Tile-AI, with TileLang's LICENSE file next to them.
- nvidia-sm120/vllm032-port/hk/horizon_kernels/gdn_round_ops/chunk_delta_h.py and chunk_delta_h_v032.py are
  copied from vLLM (Apache-2.0, Copyright contributors to the vLLM project), which took them from
  flash-linear-attention (MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2025 Songlin Yang, Yu Zhang). Their original SPDX and MIT
  headers are kept. They are source inputs for vLLM's vendored flash-linear-attention build: their relative imports
  (.index, .op, .utils) resolve only inside that package, so they do not import from this tree.
- nvidia-sm120/patches/*.patch and nvidia-sm120/docs/upstream/*.patch are diffs against vLLM (Apache-2.0,
  Copyright contributors to the vLLM project) and contain vLLM context lines.
- nvidia-sm120/docs/upstream/vllm-fla-blackwell-warps.patch changes vLLM's vendored copy of
  flash-linear-attention (vllm/third_party/flash_linear_attention/ops/); its context lines are MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2023-2025 Songlin Yang, Yu Zhang.
- nvidia-sm120/results/stable_align_28-09-2026/*.cu are CUDA sources generated by the TileLang compiler (MIT,
  Copyright (c) Tile-AI), including TileLang's prelude, from our stable-alignment kernel; kept as a record.
- amd-mi250x/experiments/n4/src/pad_8k.cu and rs2_8k.cu are HIP sources generated by the TileLang compiler (MIT,
  Copyright (c) Tile-AI) and then edited by hand for the experiment.
- amd-mi250x/kernels/gqa_fa.py embeds HIP source (the form J/JTP templates) that the TileLang compiler (MIT,
  Copyright (c) Tile-AI) generated from our kernel and that was then edited by hand; it also carries the RegVec
  helper of TileLang patch 0007.
- amd-mi250x/experiments/e2/e2run.py follows the call sequence of fused_experts_impl in vLLM's fused_moe.py
  (Apache-2.0, Copyright contributors to the vLLM project); experiments/e2/e2k.py and kernels/moe_fused.py
  re-implement vLLM's two-block MoE alignment idea in TileLang.
